<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
The unqualified GNU license aliases in <code>lib.licenses</code> — such as
<code>gpl2</code>, <code>gpl3</code>, <code>lgpl2</code>, <code>lgpl21</code>,
and <code>lgpl3</code> — are deprecated. They are ambiguous because the name
alone does not say whether the package is licensed under that exact version
(<code>Only</code>) or under that version or any later version
(<code>Plus</code>).
</p>
<p>
Leaving the alias ambiguous makes reviews harder and can encode the wrong legal
meaning in <code>meta.license</code>.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Replace the deprecated alias with the matching unambiguous one, such as
<code>gpl3Only</code> or <code>gpl3Plus</code>. Determine which variant applies
from the project's README, website, or source-file license headers; if the
terms are still unclear, ask upstream to clarify them.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Problematic — deprecated ambiguous aliases:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, lib }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  meta.license = with lib.licenses; [ gpl3 mit ];
}
</sample>
<p>Recommended — use an explicit <code>Only</code> or <code>Plus</code> alias:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, lib }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  meta.license = with lib.licenses; [ gpl3Only mit ];
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/unclear-gpl.md"><code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>unclear-gpl</code></a>
</li>
<li>
GNU: <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/identify-licenses-clearly.html">How to use GNU licenses for your own software</a>
</li>
<li>
Nixpkgs deprecation discussion:
<a href="https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/92348">PR #92348</a>,
<a href="https://discourse.nixos.org/t/lib-licenses-gpl3-co-are-now-deprecated/8206">Discourse thread</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
